It's crazy, it's--


01:14:48.635 --> 01:14:51.731
What kind of movie?
Uh, it's a tragedy.


01:14:51.839 --> 01:14:56.003
But you are laughing.
Yeah, well, it's a tragic comedy.


01:14:57.644 --> 01:15:00.979
So, um, what is
the title of your movie?


01:15:02.415 --> 01:15:04.009
Bill's


01:15:06.353 --> 01:15:08.186
Awfully Amazing Adventure.


01:15:08.256 --> 01:15:12.989
Oh, yeah, that's a very
typical American title.


01:15:13.060 --> 01:15:15.030
Oh, yeah?
Yeah.


01:15:15.096 --> 01:15:17.156
Oh, you didn't like it?
No.


01:15:17.231 --> 01:15:18.860
You got something better?
Yes.


01:15:18.934 --> 01:15:21.199
Okay, what is it?


01:15:21.269 --> 01:15:24.330
How about, um,


01:15:27.276 --> 01:15:29.711
Big Story in a Small Village.


01:15:29.778 --> 01:15:33.179
Oh, okay, that's a little
too Armenian.


01:15:33.247 --> 01:15:35.376
Oh, okay.


01:15:35.451 --> 01:15:38.854
How about...Lost?


01:15:38.922 --> 01:15:41.049
That's so dumb.
Why?


01:15:41.123 --> 01:15:44.389
Because it is a American TV show.


01:15:44.460 --> 01:15:46.293
Yeah, you're right.
Yes.


01:15:46.363 --> 01:15:48.525
It was good though.
Yeah, it was good.


01:15:48.598 --> 01:15:51.295
You know, the fifth season
is very confusing.


01:15:51.368 --> 01:15:52.733
Yeah, people say that.


01:15:55.271 --> 01:15:56.603
How about


01:15:58.542 --> 01:16:00.032
Lost and Found?


01:16:00.110 --> 01:16:03.877
Why would it be called
Lost and Found?


01:16:03.947 --> 01:16:08.079
<i>Because it's a story
about a guy who's lost.</i>


01:16:08.152 --> 01:16:11.144
And during his adventure,
he finds what he is looking for.


01:16:11.221 --> 01:16:14.454
And you have found
what you're looking for?


01:16:18.296 --> 01:16:20.595
Not yet.


01:16:20.665 --> 01:16:24.295
So then why would it be titled
Lost and Found?


01:16:27.672 --> 01:16:29.834
'Cause the story isn't finished.


01:16:55.001 --> 01:16:57.164
What the hell is his problem?
What does he want from me?


01:17:35.311 --> 01:17:36.836
What is wrong with that guy?


01:17:36.911 --> 01:17:38.574
Oh, God, nothing.


01:17:38.647 --> 01:17:39.841
He's a psycho.
No.


01:17:39.914 --> 01:17:41.576
No, he's insane.
No, no.


01:17:41.649 --> 01:17:44.085
He's such a sweet old man.
He's harmless.


01:17:44.186 --> 01:17:47.247
Harmless my ass.
Guy's a sadist.


01:17:51.227 --> 01:17:52.422
Jeez.


01:17:56.365 --> 01:17:58.096
Okay.


01:17:58.201 --> 01:18:00.260
Listen.


01:18:00.336 --> 01:18:03.273
Can I just--
Can I just stay here tonight?


01:18:03.373 --> 01:18:05.434
I mean, right here.


01:18:05.543 --> 01:18:07.170
I promise I won't bother you.


01:18:07.244 --> 01:18:09.213
I'll be gone before your mother
gets up.


01:18:09.279 --> 01:18:10.611
Okay.


01:18:10.714 --> 01:18:13.275
<i>Okay?
Okay.</i>


01:18:13.384 --> 01:18:18.618
But we have to wake up early because I would 
like to visit my father's grave site, okay?


01:18:18.723 --> 01:18:21.022
Okay.
Okay.


01:18:26.697 --> 01:18:28.962
You mind if I tag along?


01:18:29.066 --> 01:18:32.731
Tag along?
I mean, um, do you mind if I come with you?


01:18:32.804 --> 01:18:34.773
Oh...no.


01:18:36.141 --> 01:18:38.700
Okay.
Okay.


01:18:38.776 --> 01:18:40.439
<i>Ani?</i>


01:18:41.547 --> 01:18:42.810
Thanks.


01:18:42.881 --> 01:18:44.646
You're welcome.


01:19:05.004 --> 01:19:07.099
It was 1991.


01:19:07.174 --> 01:19:10.769
I was eight when my father
died during the war with the Azeris.


01:19:12.313 --> 01:19:15.147
He and my cousin Ashad.
Ashad was 15.


01:19:17.751 --> 01:19:20.016
<i>Twenty-eight people.</i>


01:19:20.120 --> 01:19:23.182
<i>Twenty-eight people died
protecting our village.</i>


01:19:24.992 --> 01:19:28.451
Grandpa Matsak lost both his sons
in one day.


01:19:28.529 --> 01:19:32.626
And two days later,
Alexan's brother was killed.


01:19:37.439 --> 01:19:39.533
Now I know why the people here
are so enraged.


01:19:39.641 --> 01:19:41.975
We are not enraged.


01:19:44.379 --> 01:19:49.215
All our lives we have fought
with Muslim countries for our land,


01:19:49.284 --> 01:19:51.720
and we have paid for it
with our blood,


01:19:51.821 --> 01:19:54.985
and no one can take it
away from us.


01:19:55.057 --> 01:19:57.822
The Azeris are just on the other side
of the mountain.


01:19:57.893 --> 01:20:00.829
<i>Do you see the wire that extends 
from mountain to mountain?</i>


01:20:00.896 --> 01:20:05.130
We put them there to stop enemy planes
from flying too low.


01:20:05.202 --> 01:20:08.228
<i>And when the war started,
I was a little girl.</i>


01:20:08.337 --> 01:20:11.502
At night it was
my responsibility to--


01:20:54.420 --> 01:20:56.446
Hey!


01:20:56.555 --> 01:20:57.614
Hey!


01:21:02.294 --> 01:21:05.732
<i>Hey! Hey!</i>


01:21:05.799 --> 01:21:07.791
Come back!


01:21:09.069 --> 01:21:10.297
Hey!


01:24:38.956 --> 01:24:40.619
Oh, what the fu--


01:24:40.692 --> 01:24:42.524
Oh, my God.


01:28:01.636 --> 01:28:02.695
Stop!


01:28:04.239 --> 01:28:05.708
Get off of her or I will shoot.


01:28:07.208 --> 01:28:09.233
Stay down or I will shoot.


01:28:10.745 --> 01:28:12.737
Stay back!


01:28:12.814 --> 01:28:14.147
Stop! Stop!


01:30:11.006 --> 01:30:12.371
<i>Buongiorno, signore.
Buongiorno.</i>


01:30:39.802 --> 01:30:41.668
Wait, what's he saying?


01:30:41.737 --> 01:30:44.002
<i>He is saying that
you are very brave,</i>


01:30:44.073 --> 01:30:47.305
and that we respect you
for what you did.


01:30:48.578 --> 01:30:50.308
Really?
Yes.


01:30:50.380 --> 01:30:51.642
<i>Tell him I said thank you.</i>


01:30:53.350 --> 01:30:56.219
You're a good man, Mr. Matsak.
Thank you.


01:32:25.680 --> 01:32:27.808
War.


01:32:41.464 --> 01:32:43.092
Okay, all right.


01:32:43.166 --> 01:32:44.293
All right.


01:33:34.752 --> 01:33:37.312
Hi.
Hi.


01:33:41.560 --> 01:33:45.088
This is a gift from our village.


01:33:48.033 --> 01:33:50.025
Thank you.


01:33:50.102 --> 01:33:52.868
Hi, this is my seat.


01:33:55.008 --> 01:33:56.873
<i>Oh, thank you.</i>


01:34:14.195 --> 01:34:15.787
I hate awkward silences.


01:34:15.896 --> 01:34:17.866
Me, too.


01:34:17.932 --> 01:34:21.734
I wish I could just take you back 
to California with me.


01:34:21.803 --> 01:34:24.794
Show you we have a lot of 
great historical sites, too.


01:34:24.905 --> 01:34:27.899
Disneyland, Starbucks,


01:34:27.975 --> 01:34:30.878
El Pollo Loco.


01:34:32.814 --> 01:34:34.907
<i>That's nice,</i>


01:34:36.050 --> 01:34:37.815
but I can't.


01:34:37.886 --> 01:34:40.219
Why not?


01:34:41.791 --> 01:34:44.156
<i>Because my everything is here.</i>


01:34:44.258 --> 01:34:48.425
<i>My mother, my village, my friends, my school.
Everything is here.</i>


01:34:48.498 --> 01:34:50.797
<i>Ladies and gentlemen,</i>


01:34:50.900 --> 01:34:53.733
<i>now please fix the back of your seats
to the upright position</i>


01:34:53.802 --> 01:34:55.168
and fasten your seatbelt.


01:34:55.237 --> 01:34:58.675
Okay, well, I guess,


01:34:58.775 --> 01:35:00.608
I guess this is it.


01:35:00.678 --> 01:35:02.771
I guess.


01:35:36.815 --> 01:35:38.944
Goodbye.
Bye.

